# SpeechLLm — speech services configuration (template).
#
# Copy to `.env` NEXT TO THIS FILE:
#     cp SpeechLLm/.env.example SpeechLLm/.env
#
# This file did not exist until 19-08, which meant the one variable that hard-
# fails had nothing announcing it: a new clone raised ValueError from a
# constructor and there was no document to check against.
#
# Note the current service does NOT use these. Vietnamese TTS moved to
# VieNeu-TTS (CPU, see agenticRAG configs/models.yaml) and ElevenLabs and Coqui
# were both replaced. Everything below serves SpeechLLm's own scripts and tests.


# ── ElevenLabs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED by src/services/elevenlabs_client.py — its constructor raises
# ValueError when this is unset, before any request is made. There is no
# offline or mock mode.
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=


# ── Coqui TTS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Force GPU on or off. Unset means "decide from torch.cuda.is_available()",
# which is what you usually want — set it only to overrule that, e.g. to keep
# the GPU free for Kimodo while still running Coqui on CPU.
# Values: "true" | "false" (case-insensitive).
# COQUI_USE_GPU=false

# Windows only: absolute path to libespeak-ng.dll. Coqui's phonemizer looks in
# the usual Program Files locations first and only consults this when they miss,
# so set it for a non-standard eSpeak NG install.
# PHONEMIZER_ESPEAK_LIBRARY=C:\Program Files\eSpeak NG\libespeak-ng.dll
